 "text": "But first the Marines had to take the heights above the pass. On the night of December eighth a battalion of the First Marines climbed toward a peak called Hill ten-eighty-one in a blinding blizzard. They attacked Chinese positions in the snow. The fighting lasted into the next day. When it ended the high ground belonged to the Marines.",
